  "instructions": [
    "Boil the white sauerkraut for about 5 minutes to soften it slightly.",
    "Season the chicken with salt and pepper on both sides. Heat oil in a wok or large skillet over medium-high heat.",
    "Add the chicken, onion, and garlic to the heated oil, stirring occasionally until the chicken is browned on all sides (about 8-10 minutes).",
    "Stir in tomato paste, Worcestershire sauce, fish sauce if using, soy sauce, and water. Bring to a simmer, then reduce heat to low.",
    "Add the sauerkraut, salt, and pepper. Stir until the chicken is cooked through and the sauce has thickened (about 5-7 minutes).",
    "Serve hot as a side dish or main course."
